msgid "``const struct sock *sk``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:317: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:737
msgid ""
"Socket object (never NULL), read without a socket lock, so its fields are a "
"best-effort snapshot.  The denied endpoint is not available: the hook runs "
"before :manpage:`bind(2)` / :manpage:`connect(2)` sets the socket addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:317: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:742
msgid "``__u64 sport``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:317: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:741
msgid ""
"Source port in host endianness, set for bind denials (zero for an autobind/"
"ephemeral port); zero for connect and send denials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:317: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:744
msgid "``__u64 dport``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:317: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:743
msgid ""
"Destination port in host endianness, set for connect and send denials; zero "
"for bind denials, and also zero for a UDP send to an AF_UNSPEC address on an "
"IPv6 socket (indistinguishable from a real destination port 0).  The bind-vs-"
"connect direction is given by **blockers**, not by which port is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:317: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:748
msgid "Emitted when a Landlock domain denies a network operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:317: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:750
msgid ""
"The port fields are converted from the socket's network byte order to host "
"endianness before emitting."
msgstr ""

